  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts and it passes typecheck. I haven't run `vite build` or loaded the page in a browser, so the rendering is unchecked. The scene has a 260×260 ground plane and three instanced nodes: 8,000 trunks, 8,000 canopies and 2,000 rocks. Placement comes from a fixed-seed LCG (seed 12345), so the forest is the same on every load. Canopies get a random green HSL colour per instance and rocks a random grey. Both use a white base material, because instance colours multiply the material colour. The scene has one shadow-casting directional light, a hemisphere light, and exponential fog (`mode: \"exp\"`, density 0.0045). The orbit camera auto-rotates slowly (0.12 rad/s) from about 155 units away, which should keep the whole 75-radius forest in view. The code sets `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` from the first `onFrame` callback, so I haven't confirmed that callback fires after the first frame is actually drawn.",
